ndary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le16ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "concierge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an employee at a hotel who gives help and information to the people staying at the hotel"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The concierge gave the tour group directions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you travel."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "authentic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "real or genuine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We went to an authentic noodle shop."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tile"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a flat piece of hard clay or stone you use to cover walls or floors"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't slip on the tile floor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come or go down quickly from a high place or position"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally fell on the stairs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "floor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the part of a room on which you stand"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally spilled her coffee on the floor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sore"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling or affected by pain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My feet are sore from walking all day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where little or no light can be seen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally had a shower in the dark."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on the house"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when a business (hotel, restaurant) gives something for free"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here is an umbrella on the house."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Homonyms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Homonyms, or multiple meaning words, have the same spelling and the same pronunciation but have different meanings.  <br/><br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\">trip</span>, <span class=\"italic\">fall</span> and <span class=\"italic\">shower</span>.<br><br>There is a type of homonyms in which you write and pronounce the words exactly the same way, but the meanings are totally different. These are known as <span class=\"strong\">homographs</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sally is on a trip to China. (noun: a journey to a place) <br/>Sally tripped on the stairs. (verb: to cause to fall or almost fall)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is a nice fall day. (noun: the season when leaves fall from trees)   <br/>I don't want to fall on the wet floor. (verb: to go down to a lower position)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had a shower at 8 o'clock. (noun: a bath with water) <br/>There were a lot of showers today. (noun: a fall of rain)"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing Uncertainty"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "If you are not sure whether something can or can not happen, you can use: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Rising intonation</span> makes you sound uncertain about what you're saying. Uncertainty can also have <span class=\"strong\">falling intonation</span>.  It depends on the speaker."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rising Intonation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Falling Intonation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Using: \u201c<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Well, \u2026</span>\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Using: \u201c<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I suppose\u2026 but\u2026</span>\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm not sure.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's impossible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I doubt it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It might be.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have my doubts.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It might not be.\\\"}\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find 5 new homonyms online or in a dictionary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences using the same word two times. Example:<span class=\"italic\"> My great-grandfather was a great man.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find homonyms on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 5 sentences using homonyms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice saying homonyms aloud."}]}], "type": "sena"}